  "notes": "Campaign definitions for the territory map. A campaign is a temporary field push - a blitz, a sweep, a promo - and is deliberately NOT a zone: zones are the ownership record and are re-stamped onto every address row nightly by the Apps Script. Each campaign lists the ZIPs that make up its area; a pin inside one of those ZIPs belongs to the campaign area. The 'campaign' column in addresses_master marks the rows that came from the campaign's own lead list, which the map draws larger than the doors it already had in the same ZIPs. Unlike zones.json this file is read ONLY by index.html - there is no Drive copy and the Apps Script does not use it.",
